  "findings": [
    "Five of six original Store opening regressions fail before correction: already-cancelled opening is admitted, zero timeout leaves state, physical client admission ignores cancellation for1.9400714s, schema lock ignores cancellation for3.1331248s, and a120ms inherited ceiling permits3.1976735s of opening.",
    "Store opening now inherits a full-Duration absolute host deadline before creating state and shares it across both client locks and SQLite schema/identity work. SQLite busy/progress policy is installed before the first statement and cleared on successful opening.",
    "Final seven opening tests pass, including zero/MAX durations without panic/state, pre-cancelled opening, both lease files, actual rollback-journal reader exclusion, inherited ceiling/cancellation, recovery, exact workspace/Unicode data after brief contention and discarded setup policy after successful opening.",
    "The owned Windows Git probe explicitly selects core.filemode=true and reproduces an index100755/worktree100644 discrepancy plus the same checkout refusal as hosted macOS. It is not a Unix emulator or Unix runtime validation.",
    "The fixture now sets the physical executable mode on Unix before staging and asserts clean tracked bytes/modes before capture/checkout. No force checkout, filemode-disable flag or test gate bypass is added. All13 mapping tests pass on Windows; actual Unix branch validation remains pending.",
    "All18 selected final native result groups execute. The only two failures are unchanged real symlink fixture creation OS1314 in federation and maintenance. Original RED logs are development traces; the final unchanged-source manifest is the authoritative final input set.",
    "Other raw SQLite connections, Unix guarded installation, macOS runtime/PDF issues, provider discussion/handoff, broader STATUS/R1-R9 and full native/platform acceptance remain separate."
  ],
